# Licensing and attribution

Original prim-hrtf code and documentation are released under the [Unlicense](UNLICENSE),
the same as Prim. That grant covers only material the author owns. The files below
carry other terms, and the SPDX expression in `Cargo.toml` is `Unlicense AND Apache-2.0`.

| Material | Terms |
| --- | --- |
| `src/eval.rs`, and the phase-unwrapping and spectrum code in `src/format.rs` | Ports of Steam Audio 4.8.1 (`hrtf_map.cpp`, `hrtf_database.cpp`), Copyright 2017-2023 Valve Corporation, Apache-2.0. These files are derivative works and stay Apache-2.0; see [LICENSE-APACHE](LICENSE-APACHE) and [NOTICE](NOTICE). |
| `data/cipic_124.phrtf` | CIPIC HRTF database, subject 124 (see below), baked and resampled by `tools/sofa2phrtf.py`. Its source file is Steam Audio's `core/data/hrtf/cipic_124.sofa`. |
| Rust dependencies | `realfft` (MIT), `rustfft`, `num-complex`, `num-integer`, `num-traits`, `primal-check`, `strength_reduce`, `transpose`, `autocfg` (each MIT OR Apache-2.0). Checked with `cargo metadata` on 2026-11-11. |
| `bench/mumble/` | `harness.cpp` is original. `build.sh` compiles Mumble's `HrtfSpatializer` and `3rdparty/fftconvolver` from a local Mumble checkout at bench time; none of that code is in this repository. Mumble is BSD-3-Clause (Copyright The Mumble Developers), fftconvolver is MIT (Copyright 2017 HiFi-LoFi), libmysofa is BSD-3-Clause (Copyright 2016-2017 Symonics GmbH, Christian Hoene). |
| LibriSpeech test-clean | Not in this repository. `tools/fetch_speech.py` downloads it at bench time from openslr.org. CC BY 4.0, Panayotov, Chen, Povey and Khudanpur (ICASSP 2015), with recordings from LibriVox volunteers (public domain). |

## CIPIC HRTF database

`data/cipic_124.phrtf` is derived from the CIPIC HRTF database (subject 124), which the
Steam Audio repository redistributes under Apache-2.0 and the Mumble tree shipped as
`default.sofa`. The CIPIC terms, copied from the SOFA file's metadata:

> The Regents of the University of California hereby grant users permission to
> reproduce and/or use materials available therein for any purpose - educational,
> research or commercial. However, each reproduction of any part of the materials must
> include the copyright notice, if it is present. In addition, as a courtesy, if these
> materials are used in published research, this use should be acknowledged in the
> publication. If these materials are used in the development of commercial products,
> the Regents of the University of California request that written acknowledgment of
> such use be sent to: CIPIC - Center for Image Processing and Integrated Computing,
> University of California, 1 Shields Avenue, Davis, CA 95616-8553.

Citation: V. R. Algazi, R. O. Duda, D. M. Thompson and C. Avendano, "The CIPIC HRTF
Database," Proc. 2001 IEEE Workshop on Applications of Signal Processing to Audio and
Electroacoustics, pp. 99-102, Mohonk Mountain House, New Paltz, NY, Oct. 21-24, 2001.

## Notices kept for ported or compared code

This crate's renderer was first written as a port of Mumble's libmysofa-based
evaluator (replaced; still in git history), so the notices of Mumble and libmysofa are
kept here.

